name: Context catalog receipts preserve Setup while recorded repository context resumes Map
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY GOOGLE_API_KEY GEMINI_API_KEY AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=0 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_catalog_startup.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 READY THE MAP RUN | fresh-setup
expect: Start Map
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_catalog_startup.py @TMP_TARGET @ART fresh
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_catalog_startup.py @TMP_TARGET @ART catalog
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 READY THE MAP RUN | catalog-remains-setup
expect: Start Map
resize: 160x48
wait: 0.3
live-snap: catalog-setup-160x48
resize: 96x89
wait: 0.3
live-snap: catalog-setup-96x89
resize: 80x24
wait: 0.3
live-snap: catalog-setup-80x24
resize: 60x20
wait: 0.3
live-snap: catalog-setup-60x20
resize: 40x12
wait: 0.3
live-snap: catalog-setup-40x12
ask: Does a completed empty context listing leave normal Setup visible across the viewport sizes, without claiming a completed Map or starting work?
resize: 120x36
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_catalog_startup.py @TMP_TARGET @ART index
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=0 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 Viewing Map | recorded-context-resumes-map
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_catalog_startup.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 25 READY THE MAP RUN | explicit-setup-still-available
ask: Does real runtime-free repository context resume its durable Map page on no-color restart while acceptance remains incomplete and explicit Setup remains available?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-planning-exit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
